      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "| καὶ ἐπηρώτησαν αὐτὸν οἱ οἰκοδομοῦντες, ἐκ τίνος ὄρους θέλῃ ἐνεχθῆναι λίθους καὶ ἐμβληθῆναι εἰς τὸν τόπον αὐτῶν. | καὶ ἐκ μὲν τῶν ὀρέων οὐκ ἐκέλευσεν ἐνεχθῆναι, | ἐκ δέ τινος πεδίου ἐγγὺς ὄντος ἐκέλευσεν ἐνεχθῆναι. |",
          "english_quote": "The supplied bounded evidence does not establish the passage-specific Athos, Palatina, or Ethiopic readings.",
          "issue": "This disclosure fails to distinguish missing direct verification from supplied passage-specific reports. The expanded evidence expressly reports that Lake Plate XI lacks the replacement question and nearby-field commands and that Palatina 209 contains corresponding instructions. The note correctly identifies the two supplements and the intervening unsupplemented negation, but its final sentence obscures the available Athos and Palatina reports by grouping them with the unestablished Ethiopic reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed replacement for fresh review: “The supplied project comparison reports that Lake’s Athos transcription lacks these supplements and that printed Palatina 209 contains corresponding instructions. These are edition-mediated reports, not fresh manuscript verification; a passage-specific Ethiopic comparison is not supplied.”",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐκέλευσε οὖν πάντας τούτους ἐκ τοῦ πύργου μετενεχθῆναι καὶ τεθῆναι παρὰ τὸν πύργον, καὶ ἑτέρους ἐνεχθῆναι λίθους καὶ ἐμβληθῆναι εἰς τὸν τόπον αὐτῶν.",
          "english_quote": "Preserve the narrated opportunity for fitting rejected stones without adding later procedures; expose editorial supplements and unresolved wording.",
          "issue": "The theological rationale attributes a narrated opportunity for fitting rejected stones to this section. The unsound stones removed in paragraph 5 are replaced; this section does not state that they will be fitted back into the building. The future cutting and placement in paragraph 8 concern the newly brought round stones withheld from immediate placement. The metadata conflates these distinct groups.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed correction for fresh review: “Preserve the removal and replacement of unsound stones and the separate provision for later cutting and placement of the newly brought round stones; expose editorial supplements and unresolved wording.”",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": false,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐκ μὲν τῶν ὀρέων οὐκ ἐκέλευσεν ἐνεχθῆναι, | ἐκ δέ τινος πεδίου ἐγγὺς ὄντος ἐκέλευσεν ἐνεχθῆναι.",
          "english_quote": "He told them to bring stones from a nearby field instead of the mountains.[c]",
          "issue": "The source separately asserts that he did not order stones brought from the mountains and that he ordered them brought from the nearby field. “Instead of” compresses this into a positive alternative command, leaving the explicit negation of the mountain order implicit. This also makes the preserved clause and the editorially supplied field command less distinguishable than the note suggests.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed replacement for fresh review: “He did not order stones brought from the mountains. He ordered them brought from a nearby field.[c]” Retain the note’s distinction between the preserved negative clause and the supplied field command.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐτέθησαν δὲ παρὰ τὸν πύργον, ὡς μελλόντων αὐτῶν λατομεῖσθαι καὶ τίθεσθαι εἰς τὸν οἰκοδομήν",
          "english_quote": "They were placed beside the tower to be cut and used later, because they were very bright.",
          "issue": "“Used later” omits the specified future action and destination: the round stones are to be placed into the building, not merely used in some unspecified way.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed replacement for fresh review: “They were placed beside the tower to be cut and put into the building later, because they were very bright.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "| καὶ ἐπηρώτησαν αὐτὸν οἱ οἰκοδομοῦντες, ἐκ τίνος ὄρους θέλῃ ἐνεχθῆναι λίθους καὶ ἐμβληθῆναι εἰς τὸν τόπον αὐτῶν. | καὶ ἐκ μὲν τῶν ὀρέων οὐκ ἐκέλευσεν ἐνεχθῆναι, | ἐκ δέ τινος πεδίου ἐγγὺς ὄντος ἐκέλευσεν ἐνεχθῆναι. |",
          "english_quote": "The supplied bounded evidence does not establish the passage-specific Athos, Palatina, or Ethiopic readings.",
          "issue": "The supplied expanded evidence includes passage-specific project reports concerning Athos and Palatina: Lake Plate XI reportedly lacks the replacement question and nearby-field commands, while Palatina 209 reportedly contains corresponding instructions. The note does not accurately distinguish these available edition-mediated reports from the missing Ethiopic comparison and absent fresh manuscript verification.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed replacement for fresh review: “The supplied project comparison reports that Lake’s Athos transcription lacks these supplements and that printed Palatina 209 contains corresponding instructions. These are edition-mediated reports, not fresh manuscript verification; a passage-specific Ethiopic comparison is not supplied.”",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐκέλευσε οὖν πάντας τούτους ἐκ τοῦ πύργου μετενεχθῆναι καὶ τεθῆναι παρὰ τὸν πύργον, καὶ ἑτέρους ἐνεχθῆναι λίθους καὶ ἐμβληθῆναι εἰς τὸν τόπον αὐτῶν.",
          "english_quote": "Preserve the narrated opportunity for fitting rejected stones without adding later procedures; expose editorial supplements and unresolved wording.",
          "issue": "The metadata conflates the removed unsound stones with the newly brought round stones awaiting cutting. Only the latter receive an explicit prospect of future placement in this section; refitting the removed unsound stones is not narrated here.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed correction for fresh review: “Preserve the removal and replacement of unsound stones and the separate provision for later cutting and placement of the newly brought round stones; expose editorial supplements and unresolved wording.”",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions require revision. The standard reader text covers the selected source faithfully, but both editions have defective evidence disclosure and metadata that conflates distinct stone groups. The simplified text additionally makes an explicit negation implicit and omits the round stones’ specified future placement into the building. The bounded “three times” selection and its disclosed count-free alternative are compatible with the supplied reports and should not be replaced merely because the alternative exists. This is a model review of the supplied source and reports, not manuscript authentication or exhaustive collation; all proposed corrections require fresh review."
}
